    "body": "Cc @aleventhal, who championed `aria-keyshortcuts`.\r\n\r\n`accesskey` isn't used consistently b/c assistive technology and internationalization contexts (inc different keyboard layouts, for example numbers on the shift plane) make it challenging to associate these with a single, simple modifier. In short, all the keys are taken or blocked in some context or another.\r\n\r\n`aria-shortcuts` is a slight improvement because it's not limited to the browser's reserved modifier for `accesskey` (usually Opt/Alt). The shortcut can be an unmodified key (e.g. \"c\" for Gmail's \"compose new mail message\" feature), or a multi-modifier shortcut (\"Shift+Ctrl+c\"). There's no magic though; the event handling is just JavaScript. The ARIA mapping just exposes _which_ shortcut to the AT.",
